","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":37.86075,"lo":27.2535,"d":332,"ds":"Kuşadası Clock Tower is a clock tower located in Kuşadası district of Aydın province, Turkey. The tower, built in 1996, was designed with a four-storey square plan and was completed with a circular clock dial and a pyramidal roof.","wpu":"Kuşadası Clock Tower","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/Ku%C5%9Fadas%C4%B1_Saat_Kulesi.jpg/960px-Ku%C5%9Fadas%C4%B1_Saat_Kulesi.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Pygela","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":37.862209,"lo":27.263729,"d":684,"ds":"Pygela (Ancient Greek: Πύγελα) or Phygela (Φύγελα) was a small town of ancient Ionia, on the coast of the Caystrian Bay, a little to the south of Ephesus. It is located near Kuşadası, Asiatic Turkey. The ruins are right down on Pygela Plaji, \"Pygela Beach.\" They are obviously partly drowned.","wpu":"Pygela","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/b2/IONIA%2C_Phygela._Circa_350-300_BC.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"},{"n":"House of the Virgin Mary","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":37.91154,"lo":27.33406,"d":8721,"ds":"The House of the Virgin Mary (Turkish: Meryemana Evi or Meryem Ana Evi, \"Mother Mary's House\") is a Catholic shrine located on Mt. Koressos (Turkish: Bülbüldağı, \"Mount Nightingale\") in the vicinity of Ephesus, 7 kilometres (4.3 mi) from Selçuk in Turkey.","wpu":"House of the Virgin Mary","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/37/House_of_the_Virgin_Mary_%2813951299641%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/960px-House_of_the_Virgin_Mary_%2813951299641%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"}],"about":{"ds":"Ephesus ( EF-uh-suhs; Ancient Greek: Έφεσος) was an ancient Greek city on the coast of Ionia, in present-day Selçuk in İzmir Province, Turkey. It was built in the 10th century BC on the site of Apasa, a city-state that was also the capital of Arzawa, by Attic and Ionian Greek colonists. During the Classical Greek era, it was one of twelve cities that were members of the Ionian League.","wpu":"Ephesus","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/84/Ephesus_Celsus_Library_Fa%C3%A7ade.jpg/960px-Ephesus_Celsus_Library_Fa%C3%A7ade.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},"wk":"2026-10-18"}